{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "Nifty Screener Export: Sort, Filter, Validate & Deduplicate",
  "scenario": "You've exported 12 large-cap Indian equities from screener.in with sector, market cap, ROCE, P/E and debt ratios. The dataset has a duplicate row, unsorted companies, and no validation gates. Convert it to a Table, apply multi-level sorts, stack filters, flag duplicates, and validate the Sector column to stop future data-entry errors.",
  "instructions": "Apply Ctrl+T to convert the data range into a Table named 'Nifty'; sort by Sector then Market Cap descending; filter to show ROCE > 18 and P/E < 25; create a duplicate-flag column; validate the Sector dropdown; and compute the filtered average ROCE using SUBTOTAL.",
  "learning_objective": "Convert a raw dataset into a living Table, apply multi-level sorts and layered filters without destroying row integrity, flag and remove duplicates, build input validation gates, and use SUBTOTAL to read filtered totals that respond to filter changes.",
  "hints": [
    "Ctrl+T on any cell inside the data block converts it to a Table; the Table Design ribbon lets you rename it and toggle the Total Row.",
    "To sort by Sector then Market Cap, do NOT select a single column—click one cell in Sector, then Data → Sort → Add Level to stack Market Cap descending as a tiebreaker.",
    "A duplicate-flag formula is =COUNTIF($B$2:$B$13, B2)—anything > 1 is a duplicate; SUBTOTAL(109, range) is the filter-aware total (ignores hidden rows)."
  ],
